data.falsifiable_test:
Run this arm and its mode twin on the same 750 val samples. Stratify by whether min distance of k1 or k4 to a bound is below 2 GN-std.

The hypothesis is falsified under any of these outcomes:
(a) aggregate rel_l2 >= 0.0195;
(b) the posterior mean is not better than the mode in the boundary stratum (paired per-sample sign test, p<0.05);
(c) the interior-stratum difference exceeds 1%.

Also report:
- the KRR-only init rel_l2;
- the chi2 wrong-basin fraction (above the chi2_m 99% quantile);
- ESS quantiles by stratum;
- the mean signed bias of k at k>1.8.

